From: AshesTom <258768419+AshesTom@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] uxtheme: XP's link colour with the styles that name none

Purpose: links (SysLink: Security Center, Control Panel pages) are XP's
navy blue with the Windows XP style's blue and olive colours.
XP behavior: the colour of links is COLOR_HOTLIGHT; Luna's blue and olive
colours do not name it, and XP keeps HIVEDEF.INF's 0 0 128.
Wine before: the style applied before stayed: after Luna's Silver, the
links kept its 100 139 203 (and an earlier scheme's grey) in blue.
Change: in the XP session, applying a style that names no hot-tracking
colour sets 0 0 128.
Scope: the XP session (WIN4WINE_SHELL unset), when a style is applied.
---
diff --git a/dlls/uxtheme/msstyles.c b/dlls/uxtheme/msstyles.c
--- a/dlls/uxtheme/msstyles.c
+++ b/dlls/uxtheme/msstyles.c
@@ -815,6 +815,20 @@
 
 static void parse_apply_color (struct PARSECOLORSTATE* state)
 {
+    /* XP's styles name no hot-tracking colour except Luna's Silver: on XP the
+     * others keep the scheme's, HIVEDEF.INF's 0 0 128, the colour of links
+     * (SysLink); here the one of the style applied before would stay. */
+    if (win4wine_shell() == WIN4WINE_SHELL_XP && state->colorCount < ARRAY_SIZE(state->colorElements))
+    {
+        int i;
+        for (i = 0; i < state->colorCount; i++)
+            if (state->colorElements[i] == COLOR_HOTLIGHT) break;
+        if (i == state->colorCount)
+        {
+            state->colorElements[state->colorCount] = COLOR_HOTLIGHT;
+            state->colorRgb[state->colorCount++] = RGB(0, 0, 128);
+        }
+    }
     if (state->colorCount > 0)
 	SetSysColors(state->colorCount, state->colorElements, state->colorRgb);
     if (state->captionColors == 0xf)
